  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_039: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. Across the completed experiments, the architecture (multimodal + multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is consistently the strongest, and the RNA encoder is the one major variable still unexplored at this optimal setting (pca_n2000 → 0.639, scvi_n200 → 0.725). Question: config_051 is identical to config_039 except it swaps scvi_n200 for scgpt, giving a clean, controlled test of whether a generative single-cell foundation model (scgpt) yields a richer RNA representation than the variational autoencoder (scvi) in the best-performing architecture. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly extends the strongest evidence with the single remaining untested RNA encoder in the optimal configuration, maximizes the chance of finding a new best, and—if scgpt underperforms—confirms scvi_n200 as the ceiling for RNA encoding, reducing uncertainty about further RNA-side improvements. No other available configuration tests as high-value an unexplored axis under the already-validated architecture."
